import Cantilune.Pi.FMSCpoSupportedActualAgent
import Cantilune.Pi.PowerdomainUnseparated.Fubini

/-!
# Genuine supported parallel and restriction coalgebra

`FMSCpoSupportedActualAgent.supportedHeadLayer` deliberately maps parallel
and restriction to bottom.  This independent module constructs the stronger
finite-control coalgebra without changing that conservative base module.

Parallel is generated by:

* left and right native interleaving;
* lower-omega-Scott Fubini pairing of both head computations; and
* the genuine free-input/free-output synchronization kernel.

Restriction is generated by a syntax-level Table-4 fold.  It classifies the
last name of the extended world, blocks actions on the restricted subject,
extrudes a restricted output value as bound output, swaps nested fresh names,
and retains tau.  The fold is then extended over the lower powerdomain by
`mapRaw` followed by `flattenRaw`.

The resulting layers have actual one-step folds in the concrete recursive
FMS agent.  Restriction additionally uses the independently constructed
recursive terminal-coalgebra operator.  The conservative source coalgebra
still maps a nested parallel or restriction head to bottom, so this file also
gives a kernel-checked counterexample to treating its one-step parallel fold
as a recursively complete Table-5 interpretation.  It does not claim a
recursive Table-5 parallel operator or Agent-observation full abstraction.
-/

noncomputable section

